<title>TURKEY: EgyptAir jet skids off Istanbul runway, none hurt.</title>
<headline>EgyptAir jet skids off Istanbul runway, none hurt.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>An EgyptAir plane  skidded off the runway after landing at Istanbul airport on Monday but all 150 people aboard escaped unhurt, Turkey's state-run Anatolian news agency said.</p>
<p>It said the Boeing 767 from Cairo slid 50 metres (yards) off the runway and got stuck in mud after landing in wet weather at about 11 a.m. (0800 GMT). The 136 passengers and 14 crew escaped uninjured.</p>
<p>Last August another EgyptAir plane overshot the runway, caught fire and hit a taxi as it landed in Istanbul in similar wet conditions. Twenty people were injured.</p>
